I am finally in Berlin.
I am very tired from the long flight.
I have a large suitcase and my backpack.
I go through the sliding doors to the outside.
It is January and it is already evening.
It is very dark and cold.
The wind is icy.
I am looking for a taxi.
A man is standing at the exit.
He is an employee of the airport.
I go to the man.
"Good evening," I say.
"Excuse me, where is there a taxi here?"
"Good evening," says the employee.
"Are you new in Berlin?"
"Yes, I come from Mexico," I answer.
"Welcome to Germany!" he says.
"There are many taxis over there."
"Thank you very much for the help," I say.
I pull my suitcase to the taxis.
